  "title": "On Occlusions in Video Action Detection: Benchmark Datasets And Training Recipes",
  "summary": "This paper introduces five new benchmark datasets (O-UCF, O-JHMDB, OVIS-UCF, OVIS-JHMDB, and Real-OUCF) and training recipes to address occlusion challenges in video action detection, achieving 32.3% performance gains on O-UCF and 32.7% on O-JHMDB. The framework leverages neural networks to outperform existing methods and demonstrates robust occlusion models.",
